% Articles of plastics of Chapter 39: articles for the conveyance or packing
% of goods (3923), tableware, kitchenware, other household and toilet articles
% (3924), and other articles of plastics (3926). A library: it includes
% gri.le, and the scenario programs plastics_cbp.le (US rulings) and
% plastics_ebti.le (EU BTIs) include it.
%
% Text: HTSUS Revision 18 (2026), Chapter 39 notes 1, 2 and subheading note 1,
% Chapter 59 note 2(a)(5), and the terms of headings 3923, 3924 and 3926
% (https://hts.usitc.gov/); the subheadings are the six-digit HS ones.
%
% What decides between the three headings is the PRINCIPAL USE of the article
% (HTSUS Additional U.S. Rule of Interpretation 1(a): the use of the class or
% kind of goods to which it belongs). That is a judgment, recorded with who
% made it and why ("; judged", outcome last). The material is read from what
% the article is classified as (GRI 3(b), gri.le): a rake of plastic panels on
% an aluminium pole is classified as its plastic panels when those give it its
% essential character. Chapter 39 note 2 sends many articles of plastics
% elsewhere — cases of 4202, parts of footwear of 6406, toys of 9503,
% textile articles of Section XI; those headings are outside the model, and a
% claim that the article belongs there is answered by the office (gri.le).
%
% Provenance: every rule and table is labelled and cites the passage it
% encodes; the documents say where their text is (sources/), so the editor
% shows each passage and the verifier checks every quotation.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a good* is a manufactured article; undefined.
    *a thing* is made of plastics; undefined.
    *a thing* is of plastics.
    *a good* is printed with motifs; undefined.
    the printing of *a good* is *a role*; judged.
    *a thing* is of cellular plastics reinforced by a textile fabric; undefined.
    *a good* is an article of plastics.
    the principal use of *a good* is *a use*; judged.
    *a use* is a household use.
    *a good* is shaped as *a form*; undefined.
    the packing form of *a good* is *a form*.
    *a good* contains *a number* percent of *a polymer*; undefined.
    *a polymer* is a polymer of *a monomer*.
    *a monomer* is a monomer of heading *a number*.
    the share of *a monomer* in *a good* is *a number*.
    *a monomer* at *a number* percent outweighs *an other monomer* at *an other number* percent.
    the predominant monomer of *a good* is *a monomer*.
    the polymer class of *a good* is *a class*.
    the subheading for *a form* of *a class* is *a code* under table packing.
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for *a use* is *a code* under table uses.
    the subheading of *a good* is *a code*.

% GRI 6 for heading 3923: by the form of the article, and for sacks and bags
% by the polymer (Chapter 39 subheading note 1: the monomer unit that
% predominates by weight).
% the six-digit subheadings of heading 3923: boxes, sacks and bags of polymers
% of ethylene or of other plastics, carboys and bottles, spools, stoppers and
% closures, other
the table packing is, with first match, with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Articles for the conveyance or packing of goods, of plastics":
    row | form                  | class          | code
    p1  | box                   | any            | "3923.10"
    p2  | sack                  | ethylene       | "3923.21"
    p3  | sack                  | any            | "3923.29"
    p4  | bottle                | any            | "3923.30"
    p5  | spool                 | any            | "3923.40"
    p6  | closure               | any            | "3923.50"
    p7  | any                   | any            | "3923.90"

% GRI 6 for headings 3924 and 3926: by the use.
% the six-digit subheadings of headings 3924 (tableware and kitchenware;
% other) and 3926 (office or school supplies; apparel; fittings for furniture;
% statuettes and other ornamental articles; other), by the article's use
the table uses is, with first match, with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Tableware, kitchenware, other household articles and hygienic":
    row | heading | use                        | code
    u1  | 3924    | table use or kitchen use   | "3924.10"
    u2  | 3924    | any                        | "3924.90"
    u3  | 3926    | office use or school use   | "3926.10"
    u4  | 3926    | apparel                    | "3926.20"
    u5  | 3926    | furniture fittings         | "3926.30"
    u6  | 3926    | ornament                   | "3926.40"
    u7  | 3926    | any                        | "3926.90"

the knowledge base plastics includes these resources:
    gri.

the knowledge base plastics includes:

HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39 is published at "https://hts.usitc.gov/reststop/file?release=currentRelease&filename=Chapter%2039#page=3".
the text of HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39 is at "sources/hts/chapter_39.txt".
HTSUS Chapter 59 is published at "https://hts.usitc.gov/reststop/file?release=currentRelease&filename=Chapter%2059#page=1".
the text of HTSUS Chapter 59 is at "sources/hts/chapter_59.txt".

% the model covers manufactured articles of headings 3923, 3924 and 3926
rule plastics_scope:
a good is within the scope of the model
    if the good is a manufactured article.

% Chapter 39 note 1: "plastics" are the materials of headings 3901 to 3914.
% Chapter 59 note 2(a)(5): plates or sheets of cellular plastics combined with
% textile fabric present merely for reinforcing are of Chapter 39.
rule note_39_1 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "means those materials of headings 3901 to 3914":
a thing is of plastics
    if the thing is made of plastics.

rule note_59_2a5 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 59,
        confer "Plates, sheets or strip of cellular plastics, combined with textile fabric, where the textile fabric is present merely for reinforcing purposes (chapter 39)":
a thing is of plastics
    if the thing is of cellular plastics reinforced by a textile fabric.

% an article is of plastics when what it is classified as consisting of (GRI
% 3(b)) is of plastics
rule plastics_article with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "shall be classified as if they consisted of the material or component which gives them their essential character":
a good is an article of plastics
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component is of plastics.

% The headings (GRI 1), decided by principal use (Additional U.S. Rule 1(a)).
% a classification controlled by use is decided by the principal use (HTSUS
% Additional U.S. Rule of Interpretation 1(a))
rule heading_3923 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Articles for the conveyance or packing of goods, of plastics":
a good is described by heading 3923
    if the good is an article of plastics
    and the principal use of the good is packing of goods.

% a classification controlled by use is decided by the principal use (HTSUS
% Additional U.S. Rule of Interpretation 1(a))
rule heading_3924 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Tableware, kitchenware, other household articles and hygienic":
a good is described by heading 3924
    if the good is an article of plastics
    and a use is a household use
    and the principal use of the good is the use.

% "Other articles of plastics": any article of plastics.
% heading 3926: other articles of plastics and articles of other materials of
% headings 3901 to 3914
rule heading_3926 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Other articles of plastics and articles of other materials of":
a good is described by heading 3926
    if the good is an article of plastics.

% Section VII note 2: plastics printed with motifs, characters or pictorial
% representations which are not merely subsidiary to the primary use of the
% goods fall in Chapter 49. Whether the printing is merely subsidiary is the
% office's judgment.
rule note_vii_2 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "printed with motifs, characters or pictorial representations, which are not merely subsidiary to the primary use of the goods, fall in chapter 49":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading is in [3923, 3924, 3926]
    and the good is printed with motifs
    and the printing of the good is primary.

table use is a household use,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Tableware, kitchenware, other household articles and hygienic".
kitchen use is a household use,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Tableware, kitchenware, other household articles and hygienic".
household use is a household use,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Tableware, kitchenware, other household articles and hygienic".
toilet use is a household use,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "or toilet articles, of plastics".

% GRI 3(a): 3926 is the residual heading of the chapter's articles.
% heading 3926 covers articles of plastics not specified in the earlier
% headings
heading 3923 is more specific than heading 3926,
    as stated in HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation, confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description".
% heading 3926 covers articles of plastics not specified in the earlier
% headings
heading 3924 is more specific than heading 3926,
    as stated in HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation, confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description".

% GRI 6.
rule plastics_subheading_3923 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good is a code
    if the heading of the good is 3923
    and the packing form of the good is a form
    and the polymer class of the good is a class
    and the subheading for the form of the class is the code under table packing.

rule plastics_subheading_by_use with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good is a code
    if the heading of the good is a heading
    and the heading is in [3924, 3926]
    and the principal use of the good is a use
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the use is the code under table uses.

% the subheadings of heading 3923 name forms of article: boxes, sacks and
% bags, carboys and bottles, spools, closures
rule packing_form with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Boxes, cases, crates and similar articles":
the packing form of a good is a form
    if the good is shaped as the form.

% an article of heading 3923 shaped as none of the forms its subheadings name
% falls in 3923.90, other
rule packing_form_other:
the packing form of a good is other
    if it is not the case that
        the good is shaped as a form.

% Chapter 39 subheading note 1(b)(1): the monomer unit that predominates by
% weight over every other single one; units of the same subheading count
% together. Ties: the later heading (Chapter 39 note 4).
polyethylene is a polymer of ethylene,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Polymers of ethylene, in primary forms".
polypropylene is a polymer of propylene,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Polymers of propylene or of other olefins, in primary forms".
polyethylene terephthalate is a polymer of ethylene terephthalate,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Poly(ethylene terephthalate)".

ethylene is a monomer of heading 3901,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Polymers of ethylene, in primary forms:3901".
propylene is a monomer of heading 3902,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Polymers of propylene or of other olefins, in primary forms:3902".
% heading 3907 covers polyesters in primary forms
ethylene terephthalate is a monomer of heading 3907,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Poly(ethylene terephthalate)".

rule note_39_sub_1_share with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "constituent monomer units of polymers falling in the same subheading shall be taken together":
the share of a monomer in a good is a total
    if the monomer is a monomer of heading a number
    and the total is the sum of each percentage such that
        the good contains the percentage percent of a polymer
        and the polymer is a polymer of the monomer.

rule note_39_sub_1_predominance with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Polymers are to be classified in the subheading covering polymers of that monomer unit which predominates by weight over every other single comonomer unit":
the predominant monomer of a good is a monomer
    if the share of the monomer in the good is a total
    and the total > 0
    and for all cases in which
            the share of an other monomer in the good is an other total
            and it is not the case that
                the other monomer is equal to the monomer
        it is the case that
            the monomer at the total percent outweighs the other monomer at the other total percent.

rule note_39_sub_1_weight with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "which predominates by weight over every other single comonomer unit":
a monomer at a total percent outweighs an other monomer at an other total percent
    if the total > the other total.

rule note_39_4_tie with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "If no single comonomer predominates, copolymers or polymer blends, as the case may be, are to be classified in the heading which occurs last in numerical order":
a monomer at a total percent outweighs an other monomer at an other total percent
    if the total = the other total
    and the monomer is a monomer of heading a number
    and the other monomer is a monomer of heading an other number
    and the number > the other number.

% subheading 3923.21: sacks and bags of polymers of ethylene
rule polymer_class_ethylene with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Of polymers of ethylene":
the polymer class of a good is ethylene
    if the predominant monomer of the good is ethylene.

% subheading 3923.29: sacks and bags of other plastics
rule polymer_class_other with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Of other plastics":
the polymer class of a good is other polymers
    if it is not the case that
        the predominant monomer of the good is ethylene.
